[108.123243, "i", "cat > PERFORMANCE_FIX.md << 'EOF'\n# Performance Fix Summary\n\n## Problem\nJSON validator was processing at ~40 docs/sec instead of the expected 400-500 docs/sec.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `validate_document()` function was calling `preprocess_schema()` and creating a new `Draft7Validator` for EVERY document validation. With 200 test documents:\n- 200 jq subprocess calls (expensive)\n- 200 validator compilations (expensive)\n- No reuse of preprocessed schemas or compiled validators\n\n## Solution\nImplemented validator caching via `get_validator()` function:\n- Added `_validator_cache` dictionary to store compiled validators by schema path\n- Each unique schema is now only preprocessed once via jq\n- Each validator is only compiled once and reused for all documents using that schema\n- With 50 schemas and 200 documents, this reduced operations from 200 to ~50\n\n## Results\n- Before: 40.2 docs/sec\n- After: ~1420 docs/sec\n- Improvement: 35x faster\n- Target met: Yes (required 400+ docs/sec)\n\n## Code Changes\n1. Added `_validator_cache"]
[108.123277, "i", " = {}` global cache\n2. Created `get_validator(schema_path)` function to manage cached validators\n3. Modified `validate_document()` to use `get_validator()` instead of calling `preprocess_schema()` directly\nEOF\n"]
[108.123398, "o", "cat > PERFORMANCE_FIX.md << 'EOF'\r\n"]
